Go to https://developer.android.com/studio
Scroll down to download command line tools zip file.
Create a root directory named C:\Android\
Extract your downloaded ZIP. Open the extracted folder, copy all of its contents (such as the bin and lib subfolders), and paste them directly inside the above folder.
Add the above directory in the PATH variable.
sdkmanager --licenses
Install platform tools using following command
sdkmanager "platform-tools" "emulator" "platforms;android-35" "system-images;android-35;default;x86_64"
Create a Virtual device
avdmanager create avd -n TestDevice -k "system-images;android-35;default;x86_64"
Varify and boot the device
emulator -avd TestDevice
Confirm by running 
adb devices
